From 6fe2cf7a478a9435c396310a30e873aa8282f0da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Bau <david.bau@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:39:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] BIND=<del>:... written by #saveoptions cannot be read back

key2txt() spells four keys by name: <space>, <esc>, <enter> and <del>.
get_changed_key_binds(), which #saveoptions uses to write BIND lines,
writes keys with key2txt(), so a changed binding for the Delete key is
saved as "BIND=<del>:<command>".  txt2key(), which reads BIND lines,
knows the first three names but not <del>, so on the next start the
line is rejected: "Unknown key binding key '<del>'."

Accept <del> in txt2key().

Report:
https://github.com/davidbau/nethack-bugreport/tree/main/bugs/26-del-key-binding-roundtrip

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/options.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/options.c b/src/options.c
index bb0f0c800..dd4dd6222 100644
--- a/src/options.c
+++ b/src/options.c
@@ -7003,6 +7003,8 @@ txt2key(char *txt)
         return ' ';
     if (!strcmp(txt, "<esc>"))
         return '\033';
+    if (!strcmp(txt, "<del>")) /* key2txt() writes it for #saveoptions */
+        return '\177';
 
     /* handle things like \b and \7 and \mX */
     if (*txt == '\\') {
